<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.993 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.993 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.1 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due November 20 was 2.993 percent, down from 3.144 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.1 billion of 175-day T-bills due February 12, 1998 was 3.568 percent, down from 3.686 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 364-day T-bills due August 20, 1998 was 4.051 percent, up from 3.886 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$775 million of C$4.9 billion bills due August 28. (Details follow)  </p>
